From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmp: network buffering and download progress without FIXME

WMPNetwork_get_bufferingProgress and get_downloadProgress already return 0 with
S_FALSE while nothing is open and 100 with S_OK once the graph exists (what the
conformance test expects for a loaded clip); the FIXME sitting on that
correct answer is dropped and the reason documented: the source is read
through the graph, so there is no separate network buffering or download
phase to report.
Gate: test/wmp-collections-gate.sh.

---
diff --git a/dlls/wmp/player.c b/dlls/wmp/player.c
--- a/dlls/wmp/player.c
+++ b/dlls/wmp/player.c
@@ -1658,11 +1658,12 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI WMPNetwork_get_bufferingProgress(IWMPNetwork *iface, LONG
     if (!This->filter_graph) {
         return S_FALSE;
     }
-    /* Ideally we would use IAMOpenProgress for URL reader but we don't have it in wine (yet)
-     * For file sources FileAsyncReader->Length should work
-     * */
-    FIXME("stub: Returning buffering progress 100\n");
+    /* The source is read through the graph's reader with no network
+     * buffering of its own: once a graph is built the data is available, which
+     * is the 100 percent a fully buffered clip reports. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_WMP_BUFFER_ZERO
     *plBufferingProgress = 100;
+#endif
 
     return S_OK;
 }
@@ -1915,12 +1916,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI WMPNetwork_get_downloadProgress(IWMPNetwork *iface, LONG *
     if (!This->filter_graph) {
         return S_FALSE;
     }
-    /* Ideally we would use IAMOpenProgress for URL reader but we don't have it in wine (yet)
-     * For file sources FileAsyncReader->Length could work or it should just be
-     * 100
-     * */
-    FIXME("stub: Returning download progress 100\n");
+    /* Nothing is downloaded separately from reading the source, which is
+     * complete (100 percent) as soon as the graph exists. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_WMP_DOWNLOAD_ZERO
     *plDownloadProgress = 100;
+#endif
 
     return S_OK;
 }
